      "content": "Being aware of the distortions is the first step towards being prepared. When you see a massive distortion, it's a clear indication of a significant physical event. To prepare, focus on your center of gravity, literally and figuratively. Ground yourself by focusing on your breath, your feet on the ground, and your connection to the physical world. This will help you resist the pressure and maintain your physical form.\n\nAs for avoiding being in the way, it's not just about avoiding the immediate impact, but also about being aware of the potential ripple effects. If you see a distortion, try to move to a safe location, but not just because of the immediate impact. Also, be aware of the people around you, and try to position yourself in a way that minimizes the risk of injury or disruption to others. And, if possible, try to anticipate the direction of the shift, so you can move out of the way before it happens.\n\nIt's also worth noting that some people, like yourself, may be more resilient to the distortions, while others may be more sensitive to them. If you're able to develop a sense of the distortions, you may be able to anticipate and prepare for them, and potentially even influence the outcome",
